---
source: tests/stages.rs
expression: reports.report(path)
input_file: tests/fixtures/expand/doc_option_result_pages.knv
---
(def some-page "(some value)\n\nWraps a value in an `option`.\n\nAs a value, it is a function of one argument, as in `(map (iter v) some)`. In\na `match`, `(some x)` is the pattern that binds the value.\n\n(match (some 3)\n  ((some value) (+ value 1))\n  (none 0))\n=> 4\n\n(collect (map (range 1 3) some))\n=> (vec (some 1) (some 2))")
(def none-page "none\n\nHolds an `option` with no value.\n\nIn a `match`, `none` is the pattern for it.\n\n(unwrap-or none 7)\n=> 7\n\n(match (the (option i64) none)\n  ((some value) value)\n  (none 0))\n=> 0")
(def expect-page "(expect option message)\n\nReturns an `option`'s value, or panics with a message on `none`.\n\n`message` is a `(ref str)`, so borrow a `string` with `as-str`. The call\nmoves an option that is not `copy`.\n\n(expect (some \"card\") \"a card is drawn\")\n=> \"card\"")
(def unwrap-ok-page "(unwrap-ok result)\n\nReturns a `result`'s `ok` value.\n\nIt panics on `err` with the printed form of the error, so the error type\nimplements `show`. It moves a result that is not `copy`.\n\n(unwrap-ok (the (result i64 string) (ok 4)))\n=> 4")
(def map-ok-page "(map-ok result function)\n\nApplies a function to a `result`'s `ok` value.\n\nIt returns the function's result in an `ok`. For `err` the function does not\nrun, and the error passes through. A keyword such as `:age` reads that\nfield. The call moves a result that is not `copy`.\n\n(map-ok (the (result i64 string) (ok 2)) (fn (n) (* n 10)))\n=> (ok 20)\n\n(map-ok (the (result i64 string) (err (str \"bad\"))) (fn (n) (* n 10)))\n=> (err (str \"bad\"))")
